//
// Probe: the spinners and timed effects of `bund/console` (D217), the
// words among them whose bytes do not depend on timing or chance.
//
//   - **`console.typewriter`** writes the message a character at a time,
//     with no newline after.
//   - **`console.text.rainbow`** draws three passes of seven frames, each
//     from the start of the line, and ends with a newline.
//   - **`spinner.text`** and its colours print one line each; with no
//     spinner running there is no empty line before it, and a number is
//     converted.
//   - **A spinner's endings with no spinner running** consume their message
//     and print nothing.
//
// Not here: `console.spinner`, whose frames depend on timing, and
// `console.text.matrix` and `spinner.text.randomcolor`, which draw at
// random. A golden strips ANSI, so the colours are pinned by the oracle
// comparison recorded in D217, not by this file.
//
"probe: console.typewriter writes the message, with no newline" println
"typed" console.typewriter nl

"probe: console.text.rainbow draws its frames and a newline" println
"rainbow" console.text.rainbow

"probe: spinner.text and its colours print one line each" println
"plain" spinner.text
"red" spinner.text.red
"green" spinner.text.green
"blue" spinner.text.blue
"magenta" spinner.text.magenta
"cyan" spinner.text.cyan
"yellow" spinner.text.yellow
42 spinner.text

"probe: with no spinner running, the endings print nothing" println
"stopped" console.spinner.stop
"done" console.spinner.success
"failed" console.spinner.fail
"careful" console.spinner.warning
"note" console.spinner.info
"after" println
